@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each positional object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Use it when you want raw text output.
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers or objects, does not word wrap or crop the output, and does not process markup or emoji codes. It does support highlighting (via the ``highlight`` argument, which defaults to ``True``) and a basic ``style``::
+
+    >>> console.out("[bold]Hello[/bold]", [1, 2], sep=" | ", style="green")
+
+
